        <p id="baseline-notes">Loading baseline manifest...</p>
        <div id="baseline-metrics" class="metric-grid"></div>
        <p>The regression baseline uses only passing reports listed in <code>baseline-manifest.json</code>. New benchmark runs are model comparisons above the baseline table; they do not refit the baseline unless the manifest is changed deliberately.</p>
        <p id="comparison-summary">Loading comparison results...</p>
        <p>The detection estimates are rough two-sample thresholds from the observed baseline standard deviation. Smaller regressions need more repeated runs; a single run is only useful for large changes.</p>
        <ul id="thresholds" class="threshold-list"></ul>
      </section>
      <div class="toolbar">
        <input id="filter" class="filter" type="search" placeholder="Filter by mode, run id, result, model, commit, notes...">
        <div id="summary" class="summary"></div>
      </div>
      <div id="mode-filters" class="mode-filters"></div>
      <div class="section-title">
        <h2>Model Comparisons</h2>
        <span id="comparison-count" class="summary"></span>
      </div>
      <p>These runs share the fitted benchmark base but are not part of <code>baseline-manifest.json</code>. Successful rows are compared against the fitted token model; failed rows are reliability failures.</p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
